2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] Fair enough! I know the VIC-20 Programmer's Reference Guide well enough. Let me work through zero
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] page and you can verify against your copy. I'll flag symbols only where there's genuine popular
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] usage.
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] Starting from $00:
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $00 (1 byte) — Jump for USR
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $01-02 (2 bytes) — Vector for USR
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $03-04 (2 bytes) — Float-Fixed vector
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $05-06 (2 bytes) — Fixed-Float vector
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $07 (1 byte) — Search character
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $08 (1 byte) — Scan-Loss character
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $09 (1 byte) — TAB column save
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $0A (1 byte) — 0=LOAD, 1=VERIFY
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $0B (1 byte) — Input buffer pointer / Number of subscripts
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $0C (1 byte) — Default DIM flag
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $0D (1 byte) — Type: FF=string, 00=numeric
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $0E (1 byte) — Type: numeric, 80=integer, 00=floating point
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $0F (1 byte) — DATA scan / LIST quote / memory flag
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $10 (1 byte) — Subscript/FNx flag
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - 11 (1 byte) — 0=INPUT, 40=GET, $98=READ
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $12 (1 byte) — ATN sign / Comparison eval flag
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $13 (1 byte) — Current I/O prompt flag
2026-03-09 10:06:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - $14-15 (2 bytes) — Integer value
