2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] Here's how the ball movement works in Woz's Breakout:
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] • Ball Position Variables:*
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] - `X` = horizontal position (0-39)
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] - `Y` = vertical position (0-119, but divided by 3 for display)
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] - `V` = horizontal velocity (-1 left, 1 right)
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] - `W` = vertical velocity (-2 to +2)
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] • Movement Loop (Lines 50-90):*
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] 1. Calculate new position: `J = Y + W` (vertical), `I = X + V` (horizontal)
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] 2. Wall collisions: If `J` goes out of bounds (0-119), reverse `W`
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] 3. Paddle collision: If `I = 0` (left wall/paddle), calculate new trajectory based on where
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] ball hits paddle
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] 4. Brick collisions: Check `SCRN(I, K)` at new position; if not background color, brick hit
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] 5. Update display: Erase old ball, draw new ball
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] • Key Physics:*
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] - Vertical bounce: Simple `W = -W` reversal
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] - Paddle bounce: Angle depends on where ball hits paddle: `W = (K-P)*2-5`
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] - Brick hits: Ball continues horizontally (`V = ABS(V)`), brick disappears
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] - Sound effects: `PEEK(-16336)` accesses speaker click
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] • Initialization (Line 40):*
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] - Random starting angle: `W = RND(5)-2` (-2 to +2)
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] - Always starts moving left: `V = -1`
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] The ball moves in straight lines with simple integer arithmetic, bouncing only on
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] vertical/horizontal surfaces.
2026-03-10 07:58:57 [deepseek-chat] 
