2026-03-10 08:14:13 [nitro@ryzen5] the abs(v) stops ball bouncing between walls, is this different than other brick out games?
2026-03-10 08:14:17 [deepseek-chat] Yes, unusual. After brick hit, `V=ABS(V)` forces horizontal move rightward. Prevents vertical
2026-03-10 08:14:17 [deepseek-chat] "brick locking" but removes leftward brick bounces. Most versions allow full 360° bounces.
2026-03-10 08:14:17 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-10 08:16:04 [nitro@ryzen5] i think positive v moves ball to the left not the right?
2026-03-10 08:16:08 [deepseek-chat] You're correct - I had it backward. Looking at the coordinates:
2026-03-10 08:16:08 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-10 08:16:08 [deepseek-chat] - `X=0` is left wall/paddle
2026-03-10 08:16:08 [deepseek-chat] - `X=39` is right wall
2026-03-10 08:16:08 [deepseek-chat] - `V=-1` moves ball left (toward paddle)
2026-03-10 08:16:08 [deepseek-chat] - `V=1` moves ball right (away from paddle)
2026-03-10 08:16:08 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-10 08:16:08 [deepseek-chat] So `V=ABS(V)` after brick hit forces ball to move rightward (toward right wall), not leftward.
2026-03-10 08:16:08 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-10 08:20:09 [nitro@ryzen5] after collision with brick the goto 80 reverses ball direction, i understand now
2026-03-10 08:20:12 [deepseek-chat] Exactly right. Line 80: `V=-V` reverses horizontal direction after brick collision. So `ABS(V)`
2026-03-10 08:20:12 [deepseek-chat] ensures it's positive first, then reversal makes it negative - always moving left after brick hit.
2026-03-10 08:20:12 [deepseek-chat] Clever sequencing.
2026-03-10 08:20:12 [deepseek-chat] 
