2026-03-10 09:59:22 [nitro@ryzen5] how to read vic20 joy port
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] The VIC-20 joystick port is read via VIA#1 (6522) at addresses 9111 (Port A) and
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 9120 (Port B).
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] Pin Mapping
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] ╭─────────────┬────────────────┬─────────┬───────────╮
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] │  Direction  │  VIA Register  │  Bit    │  Address  │
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] ├─────────────┼────────────────┼─────────┼───────────┤
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] │  Up         │  Port A        │  bit 2  │  $9111    │
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] │  Down       │  Port A        │  bit 3  │  $9111    │
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] │  Left       │  Port A        │  bit 4  │  $9111    │
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] │  Fire       │  Port A        │  bit 5  │  $9111    │
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] │  Right      │  Port B        │  bit 7  │  $9120    │
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] ╰─────────────┴────────────────┴─────────┴───────────╯
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] All bits are active low (0 = pressed, 1 = released).
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 6502 Assembly
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] readjoy:
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6]     lda $9111       ; VIA#1 Port A
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6]     and #%00111100  ; mask bits 2-5 (up, down, left, fire)
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6]     sta joyval
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6]     lda $9120       ; VIA#1 Port B
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6]     and #%10000000  ; mask bit 7 (right)
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6]     ora joyval
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6]     eor #%10111100  ; invert so 1 = pressed
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6]     sta joyval
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6]     rts
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] joyval: .byte 0
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] After the call, `joyval` bits mean (1 = active):
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - Bit 2: Up
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - Bit 3: Down
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - Bit 4: Left
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - Bit 5: Fire
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] - Bit 7: Right
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] BASIC equivalent
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 10 A = PEEK(37137) : B = PEEK(37152)
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 20 UP = (A AND 4) = 0
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 30 DN = (A AND 8) = 0
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 40 LF = (A AND 16) = 0
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 50 FR = (A AND 32) = 0
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 60 RT = (B AND 128) = 0
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] The split across two VIA ports is a common gotcha — right is the odd one out on Port B.
2026-03-10 09:59:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:11 [nitro@ryzen5] how to read paddle buttons
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] The VIC-20 paddle buttons are read from the same VIA#1 ports as the joystick, sharing some
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] lines.
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] Paddle Button Mapping
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] ╭───────────────┬────────────────┬───────┬──────────╮
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] │  Button       │  VIA Register  │  Bit  │  Address │
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] ├───────────────┼────────────────┼───────┼──────────┤
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] │  Paddle 1 btn │  Port A        │  bit 2│  $9111   │
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] │  Paddle 2 btn │  Port A        │  bit 4│  $9111   │
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] ╰───────────────┴────────────────┴───────┴──────────╯
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] Active low (0 = pressed).
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] These are the same lines as joystick Up and Left — the VIC-20 doesn't distinguish; it's the
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] same electrical connection.
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] Paddle Analog Values (Resistance)
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] The paddle positions are read via the SID-less analog inputs routed to VIA#1 Timer.
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] The VIC-20 uses the POT lines on the control port, read through:
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] ╭───────────────┬──────────╮
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] │  Paddle 1 (X) │  $9008   │  (POT X)
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] │  Paddle 2 (Y) │  $9009   │  (POT Y)
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] ╰───────────────┴──────────╯
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] Wait — those aren't quite right. The VIC-20 doesn't have SID POT registers. The paddles are
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] actually read via:
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] $9008  -  Paddle X (analog value, 0-255)
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] $9009  -  Paddle Y (analog value, 0-255)
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] These are VIC chip registers, not VIA.
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 6502 Assembly
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] readpaddle:
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 	lda $9008       ; paddle 1 position (0-255)
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 	sta padx
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 	lda $9009       ; paddle 2 position (0-255)
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 	sta pady
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 	lda $9111       ; VIA#1 Port A
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 	and #%00000100  ; bit 2
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 	eor #%00000100  ; invert: 1 = pressed
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 	sta btn1
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 	lda $9111
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 	and #%00010000  ; bit 4
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 	eor #%00010000
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 	sta btn2
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 	rts
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] padx:	.byte 0
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] pady:	.byte 0
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] btn1:	.byte 0
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] btn2:	.byte 0
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] BASIC
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:00:27 [claude-opus-4-6] 
