2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] Paddle Button Mapping
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] ╭───────────────┬────────────────┬───────┬──────────╮
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] │  Button       │  VIA Register  │  Bit  │  Address │
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] ├───────────────┼────────────────┼───────┼──────────┤
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] │  Paddle 1 btn │  Port A        │  bit 4│  $9111   │
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] │  Paddle 2 btn │  Port B        │  bit 7│  $9120   │
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] ╰───────────────┴────────────────┴───────┴──────────╯
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] Paddle 1 button shares the joystick Left line, and Paddle 2 button shares the joystick Right line —
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] which is on the other VIA port entirely.
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 6502 Assembly
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] readpaddle:
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 	lda $9008       ; paddle 1 position
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 	sta padx
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 	lda $9009       ; paddle 2 position
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 	sta pady
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 	lda $9111       ; VIA#1 Port A
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 	and #%00010000  ; bit 4
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 	eor #%00010000
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 	sta btn1
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 	lda $9120       ; VIA#1 Port B
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 	and #%10000000  ; bit 7
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 	eor #%10000000
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 	sta btn2
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 	rts
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] That split across Port A and Port B catches people out — same gotcha as joystick Right.
2026-03-10 10:04:25 [claude-opus-4-6] 
