2026-03-10 10:06:54 [nitro@ryzen5] on vic20 can i reduce the tab size
2026-03-10 10:07:00 [claude-opus-4-6] No, the VIC-20 has a fixed tab stop every 10 columns. There's no POKE or register to change
2026-03-10 10:07:00 [claude-opus-4-6] it — it's hardcoded in the KERNAL ROM's screen editor routine.
2026-03-10 10:07:00 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:07:00 [claude-opus-4-6] Workarounds
2026-03-10 10:07:00 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:07:00 [claude-opus-4-6] - Use `SPC(n)` for custom spacing in PRINT statements
2026-03-10 10:07:00 [claude-opus-4-6] - Use string padding with spaces
2026-03-10 10:07:00 [claude-opus-4-6] - Write a custom print routine that handles your own tab character
2026-03-10 10:07:00 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:07:20 [nitro@ryzen5] can i set cursor hpos
2026-03-10 10:07:26 [claude-opus-4-6] Yes, use the POKE approach:
2026-03-10 10:07:26 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:07:26 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:07:26 [claude-opus-4-6] POKE 211, X
2026-03-10 10:07:26 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:07:26 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:07:26 [claude-opus-4-6] Where X is the column (0-21 on unexpanded screen). Follow it with a `SYS 58732` or simply `PRINT`
2026-03-10 10:07:26 [claude-opus-4-6] to update the cursor position.
2026-03-10 10:07:26 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-10 10:07:26 [claude-opus-4-6] Or use `PRINT TAB(X)` within a PRINT statement, though TAB only moves forward and is relative to
2026-03-10 10:07:26 [claude-opus-4-6] the current line.
2026-03-10 10:07:26 [claude-opus-4-6] 
