2026-03-12 08:06:45 [grok-4.20-beta] 
2026-03-12 08:06:45 [grok-4.20-beta] - If you walk → the car stays at home → you cannot wash it.
2026-03-12 08:06:45 [grok-4.20-beta] - If you drive → you can wash it.
2026-03-12 08:06:45 [grok-4.20-beta] 
2026-03-12 08:06:45 [grok-4.20-beta] The question only makes sense if you notice that the car’s location is a critical piece of
2026-03-12 08:06:45 [grok-4.20-beta] information.
2026-03-12 08:06:45 [grok-4.20-beta] 
2026-03-12 08:06:45 [grok-4.20-beta] That’s why it’s used as a test. It’s very simple, but it exposes whether an AI is actually reading
2026-03-12 08:06:45 [grok-4.20-beta] the full prompt carefully or just pattern-matching to the most obvious question.
2026-03-12 08:06:45 [grok-4.20-beta] 
2026-03-12 08:06:45 [grok-4.20-beta] You didn’t trick me.
2026-03-12 08:06:45 [grok-4.20-beta] I just failed to read properly.
2026-03-12 08:06:45 [grok-4.20-beta] 
