2026-03-12 08:25:59 [nitro@ryzen5] instances of things crashing into the moon
2026-03-12 08:26:07 [grok-4.20-beta] • Notable Things That Have Crashed Into the Moon:*
2026-03-12 08:26:07 [grok-4.20-beta] 
2026-03-12 08:26:07 [grok-4.20-beta] • Human-made impacts:*
2026-03-12 08:26:07 [grok-4.20-beta] - Luna 2 (1959) – First man-made object to crash into the Moon (Soviet Union).
2026-03-12 08:26:07 [grok-4.20-beta] - Ranger 7, 8 & 9 (1964–65) – NASA deliberately smashed these into the Moon after taking
2026-03-12 08:26:07 [grok-4.20-beta] final close-up photos.
2026-03-12 08:26:07 [grok-4.20-beta] - Apollo S-IVB stages – Multiple Saturn V third stages intentionally crashed to generate
2026-03-12 08:26:07 [grok-4.20-beta] artificial moonquakes for Apollo seismometers.
2026-03-12 08:26:07 [grok-4.20-beta] - LCROSS Centaur (2009) – NASA slammed a rocket upper stage into Cabeus crater at ~2.5 km/s
2026-03-12 08:26:07 [grok-4.20-beta] to hunt for water ice.
2026-03-12 08:26:07 [grok-4.20-beta] - 2022 Rogue Rocket – A Chinese Long March 3C booster (from the Chang’e 5 T1 mission)
2026-03-12 08:26:07 [grok-4.20-beta] slammed into the far side, creating a distinctive double crater.
2026-03-12 08:26:07 [grok-4.20-beta] 
2026-03-12 08:26:07 [grok-4.20-beta] The Moon is still getting peppered daily by small meteoroids and asteroids. The biggest ones
2026-03-12 08:26:07 [grok-4.20-beta] happened billions of years ago during the Late Heavy Bombardment, which is why the surface looks
2026-03-12 08:26:07 [grok-4.20-beta] like it lost a fight with a shotgun.
