2026-03-23 18:31:44 [nitro@ryzen5] timing of typical PAL video sync
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] PAL video sync timing is based on a 50 Hz field rate (25 frames per second). Here are the key
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] timing values:
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] • Horizontal timing (per line):*
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] - Total line duration: 64 µs
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] - Active video: ~52 µs
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] - Horizontal blanking: ~12 µs
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] - Horizontal sync pulse: 4.7 µs ± 0.2 µs
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] • Vertical timing (per frame/field):*
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] - Total lines per frame: 625 lines
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] - Active lines: 576 lines (288 per field for interlaced)
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] - Vertical blanking: 49 lines
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] - Field duration: 20 ms (1/50 second)
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] - Frame duration: 40 ms (1/25 second)
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] • Sync signals:*
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] - Horizontal sync: negative-going pulse
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] - Vertical sync: serrated pulses (5 broad pulses over 2.5 lines)
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] - Equalizing pulses: 5 pulses before and after vertical sync
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] • Color subcarrier:*
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] - Frequency: 4.43361875 MHz
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] - Phase alternates by 180° between lines (PAL characteristic)
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] These timings ensure proper synchronization between broadcast signals and television receivers in
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] PAL regions (Europe, Australia, parts of Asia/Africa).
2026-03-23 18:31:53 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:36:24 [nitro@ryzen5] describe difference between horizontal blanking and h-sync
2026-03-23 18:36:30 [deepseek-chat] • Horizontal blanking* is the entire period when the electron beam returns from the right
2026-03-23 18:36:30 [deepseek-chat] to left side of the screen. It includes:
2026-03-23 18:36:30 [deepseek-chat] - Front porch (brief delay after active video)
2026-03-23 18:36:30 [deepseek-chat] - Horizontal sync pulse (the actual timing signal)
2026-03-23 18:36:30 [deepseek-chat] - Back porch (delay before next active video starts)
2026-03-23 18:36:30 [deepseek-chat] - Color burst (on back porch for color signals)
2026-03-23 18:36:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:36:30 [deepseek-chat] • Horizontal sync* is specifically the negative-going pulse within the blanking interval
2026-03-23 18:36:30 [deepseek-chat] that tells the display exactly when to start each new scan line.
2026-03-23 18:36:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:36:30 [deepseek-chat] • Analogy:* Blanking is the entire "turnaround time" between lines; sync is the precise
2026-03-23 18:36:30 [deepseek-chat] "starting gun" within that period.
2026-03-23 18:36:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:37:52 [nitro@ryzen5] so if my ciruit waits for a ~4.7µs pulse it can then start sampling pixels for each line
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] Yes, but with important timing considerations:
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] • Correct approach:*
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] 1. Detect the falling edge of the ~4.7 µs h-sync pulse
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] 2. Wait for the back porch period (~5.8 µs typical)
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] 3. Then start sampling pixels
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] • Typical timing after h-sync falling edge:*
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] - Back porch: ~5.8 µs
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] - Color burst (if present): ~2.25 µs
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] - Active video starts: ~8-9 µs after h-sync falling edge
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] • Circuit design tips:*
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] - Use the h-sync pulse as a reset/reference for your pixel counter
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] - Add a programmable delay or counter to account for back porch
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] - Sample during the ~52 µs active video window
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] - Reset on next h-sync pulse
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] • Simple digital approach:*
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] always @(negedge h_sync) begin
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat]   pixel_counter <= BACK_PORCH_DELAY;
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat]   sampling_enable <= 0;
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] end
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] always @(posedge pixel_clock) begin
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat]   if (pixel_counter > 0)
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat]     pixel_counter <= pixel_counter - 1;
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat]   else
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat]     sampling_enable <= 1;
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] end
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] The h-sync pulse tells you when each line starts, but you need to wait through the blanking
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] interval before valid pixel data arrives.
2026-03-23 18:38:01 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:38:50 [nitro@ryzen5] how should my vsync detection work?
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] • VSYNC detection* in PAL works differently than HSYNC due to the interlaced structure:
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] • Key characteristics:*
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] - VSYNC consists of 5 broad pulses over 2.5 lines
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] - Each broad pulse is ~27.3 µs (twice normal HSYNC width)
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] - Preceded/followed by 5 equalizing pulses
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] - Occurs during vertical blanking (49 lines)
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] • Detection strategies:*
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] • 1. Pulse Width Discrimination:*
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] // Detect long pulses (~27µs vs ~4.7µs)
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] always @(negedge h_sync) begin
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat]   pulse_timer <= 0;
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] end
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] always @(posedge clock) begin
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat]   if (!h_sync)
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat]     pulse_timer <= pulse_timer + 1;
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat]   else if (pulse_timer > VSYNC_THRESHOLD)
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat]     vsync_detected <= 1;
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] end
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] • 2. Pattern Recognition (more reliable):*
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] - Look for sequence: 5 equalizing → 5 broad → 5 equalizing pulses
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] - Count 5 long pulses within ~10 lines
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] • 3. Combined HSYNC/VSYNC detection:*
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] // State machine approach
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] parameter IDLE = 0, EQ_DETECT = 1, VSYNC_DETECT = 2, POST_EQ = 3;
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] always @(negedge h_sync) begin
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat]   case(state)
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat]     IDLE: if (pulse_is_long) state <= EQ_DETECT;
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat]     EQ_DETECT: if (pulse_count == 5) state <= VSYNC_DETECT;
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat]     VSYNC_DETECT: if (pulse_count == 5) state <= POST_EQ;
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat]     POST_EQ: if (pulse_count == 5) state <= IDLE;
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat]   endcase
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] end
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] • Important notes:*
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] - VSYNC indicates start of field (not frame)
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] - Odd/even fields alternate (determined by half-line relationship)
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] - Wait ~19 lines after VSYNC ends before active video starts
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] - Reset line counter on VSYNC detection
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] • Simple approach:* Detect 3+ consecutive long pulses during expected vertical blanking
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] period (every 312.5 lines).
2026-03-23 18:39:05 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:42:02 [nitro@ryzen5] for the PAL VIC-20 computer, there is no interlace so the correct term for the signal is 50P?
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] For the PAL VIC-20: No, it's not 50P.
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] • Correct terminology: It's 288p50* (or 576i timing with progressive scan).
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] • Explanation:*
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] - Uses standard PAL timings (625 lines total, 50 Hz)
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] - But displays all 288 active lines every field (non-interlaced)
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] - Each field is identical = progressive scan
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] - Still follows PAL sync structure with serrated VSYNC
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] • Why not 50P?*
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] - 50P typically means 576p50 (full frame progressive)
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] - VIC-20 has only 288 visible lines per field
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] - Effectively half vertical resolution of full PAL
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] • Signal characteristics:*
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] - 50 fields/second (identical content each field)
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] - 288 active lines per field
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] - Uses same sync pulses as interlaced PAL
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] - CRT displays it as stable non-interlaced image
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] • Technical term:* "288-line progressive scan at 50 Hz using PAL timings" or simply "PAL
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] progressive" in retro computing contexts.
2026-03-23 18:42:11 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:05:27 [nitro@ryzen5] describe the serrated VSYNC
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] • Serrated VSYNC* is the unique vertical sync pulse structure used in interlaced video
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] standards like PAL and NTSC.
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] • Structure (PAL example):*
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] Line 1:  |-----|     |-----|     (equalizing pulses)
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] Line 2:  |-----|     |-----|
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] Line 3:  |-----|     |-----|
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] Line 4:  |-----|     |-----|
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] Line 5:  |-----|     |-----|
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] Line 6:  |-----------|           (broad pulse - 27.3µs)
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] Line 7:            |-----------|
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] Line 8:  |-----------|
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] Line 9:            |-----------|
