2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] • Key features:*
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] 1. 5 equalizing pulses (normal HSYNC width: ~4.7µs)
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] 2. 5 broad pulses (double width: ~27.3µs) over 2.5 lines
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] 3. Another 5 equalizing pulses
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] 4. Total: ~20 lines for complete VSYNC sequence
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] • Why serrated?*
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] - Maintains horizontal sync during vertical blanking
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] - Prevents horizontal oscillator from drifting
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] - Ensures proper interlace alignment (odd/even fields)
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] • Electrical characteristics:*
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] - Pulses are negative-going like HSYNC
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] - Broad pulses = 2× normal HSYNC width
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] - Equalizing pulses = normal HSYNC width
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] - Occurs during vertical blanking interval
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] • Detection clue:* Look for 3+ consecutive broad pulses during expected vertical interval
2026-03-23 19:05:44 [deepseek-chat] (every 312.5 lines in PAL).
