2026-03-23 19:13:42 [nitro@ryzen5] so for vic-20 288p50 there are 288 visible lines and 24.5 or 25 lines worth of vblank?
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] For the PAL VIC-20's 288p50 signal:
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] • Total lines per field:* 312.5 lines (half of 625)
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] • Breakdown:*
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] - Visible lines: 288 lines
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] - Vertical blanking: 24.5 lines
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] • Why 24.5 lines?*
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] - Standard PAL has 49 lines of vblank per frame
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] - VIC-20 uses progressive timing (same each field)
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] - So: 49 lines ÷ 2 fields = 24.5 lines vblank per field
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] • Field timing:*
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] - Field duration: 20 ms (50 Hz)
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] - Active video: ~18.4 ms (288 lines × 64 µs)
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] - Vertical blanking: ~1.6 ms (24.5 lines × 64 µs)
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] • Important: The 0.5 line* matters for:
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] - Maintaining correct 50 Hz field rate
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] - Proper VSYNC serration alignment
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] - CRT vertical oscillator synchronization
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] • So yes:* 288 visible + 24.5 vblank = 312.5 lines per field, matching PAL half-frame
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] timing while displaying progressive content.
2026-03-23 19:13:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:17:10 [nitro@ryzen5] what voltage is signal in vblank when not being pulsed -ve
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] In a standard 1Vpp composite video signal:
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] • During vertical blanking (between sync pulses):*
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] - Voltage: 0V (or very close to 0V)
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] - This is the blanking level or black level
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] • Signal levels reference:*
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] - Sync tip: -0.3V (negative)
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] - Blanking level: 0V (black reference)
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] - White level: +0.7V (maximum)
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] - Color burst: ±0.15V around 0V
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] • During vertical blanking interval:*
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] 1. Between equalizing/broad pulses: Returns to 0V
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] 2. No active video information present
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] 3. Only sync pulses dip below 0V
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] 4. Signal sits at blanking level (0V) most of the time
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] • Why 0V?*
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] - Defines black reference for display
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] - Ensures CRT beam is fully off between lines/fields
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] - Provides DC restoration reference point
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] • Measurement tip:* Use DC coupling on oscilloscope to see the true 0V blanking level
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] between pulses.
2026-03-23 19:17:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:19:19 [nitro@ryzen5] i am using a highspeed voltage comparator to detect sync so was hoping to just use ~0.2v to detect vblank and hblank periods
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] • Good approach*, but needs careful threshold selection:
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] • Recommended threshold: ~0.1V* (not 0.2V)
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] • Why lower is better:*
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] - Blanking level = 0V
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] - Noise margin: Keep threshold close to 0V
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] - 0.2V risks false triggers from signal overshoot/ringing
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] - Color burst swings ±0.15V around 0V
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] • Comparator setup:*
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] Reference voltage: 0.1V
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] Input: Composite video (AC-coupled)
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] Output: Digital sync signal
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] • Behavior:*
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] - Below 0.1V → Output HIGH (sync/blanking detected)
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] - Above 0.1V → Output LOW (active video)
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] • Considerations:*
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] 1. Add hysteresis (Schmitt trigger) to prevent noise chatter
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] 2. AC-couple input to remove DC offset variations
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] 3. 0.1V gives clean separation from color burst (max 0.15V)
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] 4. Sync tips go to -0.3V, so solid detection margin
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] • Alternative: Use 0.05V* for even more noise immunity while still detecting all
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] sync pulses reliably.
2026-03-23 19:19:29 [deepseek-chat] 
