2026-03-29 18:38:46 [nitro@ryzen5] bool __no_inline_not_in_flash_func(ReadBootSel)() {	const uint CS_PIN_INDEX = 1;	uint32_t flags = save_and_disable_interrupts();// Set chip select to Hi-Z	hw_write_masked(&ioqspi_hw->io[CS_PIN_INDEX].ctrl, GPIO_OVERRIDE_LOW<<IO_QSPI_GPIO_QSPI_SS_CTRL_OEOVER_LSB, IO_QSPI_GPIO_QSPI_SS_CTRL_OEOVER_BITS);	for (volatile int i = 0; i < 1000; ++i);// The HI GPIO registers in SIO can observe and control the 6 QSPI pins.	bool isDown=!(sio_hw->gpio_hi_in & (1u << CS_PIN_INDEX));	hw_write_masked(&ioqspi_hw->io[CS_PIN_INDEX].ctrl, GPIO_OVERRIDE_NORMAL<<IO_QSPI_GPIO_QSPI_SS_CTRL_OEOVER_LSB, IO_QSPI_GPIO_QSPI_SS_CTRL_OEOVER_BITS);	restore_interrupts(flags);	return isDown;}
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] The issue occurs because the RP2350 architecture changed how QSPI pins are mapped. On the RP2040,
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] the QSPI pins were accessible via the SIO block (`siohw->gpiohiin`). On the RP2350,
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] `gpiohi_in` maps to standard GPIOs 32–47, so reading it no longer targets the QSPI Chip Select
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] (CS) pin.
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] To detect the BOOTSEL button press on the RP2350, you must read the input state directly from the
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] QSPI IO status register (`INFROMPAD` bit).
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] Here is the updated, cross-compatible reusable function:
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] #include "hardware/sync.h"
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] #include "hardware/structs/ioqspi.h"
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] #include "hardware/structs/sio.h"
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] bool __no_inline_not_in_flash_func(ReadBootSel)() {
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	const uint CS_PIN_INDEX = 1;
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	uint32_t flags = save_and_disable_interrupts();
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// Set chip select to Hi-Z
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	hw_write_masked(&ioqspi_hw->io[CS_PIN_INDEX].ctrl,
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					GPIO_OVERRIDE_LOW << IO_QSPI_GPIO_QSPI_SS_CTRL_OEOVER_LSB,
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					IO_QSPI_GPIO_QSPI_SS_CTRL_OEOVER_BITS);
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// Allow time for the pad state to settle
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	for (volatile int i = 0; i < 1000; ++i);
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// Read pad state (Handles both RP2040 and RP2350)
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] #if defined(PICO_RP2040)
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	bool isDown = !(sio_hw->gpio_hi_in & (1u << CS_PIN_INDEX));
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] #else
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	bool isDown = !(ioqspi_hw->io[CS_PIN_INDEX].status & IO_QSPI_GPIO_QSPI_SS_STATUS_INFROMPAD_BITS);
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] #endif
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// Restore chip select
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	hw_write_masked(&ioqspi_hw->io[CS_PIN_INDEX].ctrl,
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					GPIO_OVERRIDE_NORMAL << IO_QSPI_GPIO_QSPI_SS_CTRL_OEOVER_LSB,
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 					IO_QSPI_GPIO_QSPI_SS_CTRL_OEOVER_BITS);
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	restore_interrupts(flags);
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	return isDown;
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] }
2026-03-29 18:40:00 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
