2026-03-29 20:29:53 [gemini-3.1-pro] Yes, moving to `out pindirs` will require a few additional setup steps, primarily in the C++
2026-03-29 20:29:53 [gemini-3.1-pro] configuration:
2026-03-29 20:29:53 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 20:29:53 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1. OUT Pin Mapping: You currently have the `SET` pins configured. You will also need to
2026-03-29 20:29:53 [gemini-3.1-pro] configure the `OUT` pin mapping to point to your video pin so the `out` instruction knows which
2026-03-29 20:29:53 [gemini-3.1-pro] GPIO to target.
2026-03-29 20:29:53 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. Shift Register Configuration: You will need to configure the Output Shift Register
2026-03-29 20:29:53 [gemini-3.1-pro] (OSR). Enabling "autopull" is highly recommended here; it allows the OSR to automatically fetch new
2026-03-29 20:29:53 [gemini-3.1-pro] data from the TX FIFO once it empties, saving you from wasting valuable PIO cycles on manual `pull`
2026-03-29 20:29:53 [gemini-3.1-pro] instructions during the active video line.
2026-03-29 20:29:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 3. FIFO Joining: Since you are only outputting data, you can configure the state machine to
2026-03-29 20:29:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] join the RX and TX FIFOs. This doubles the depth of your TX FIFO, giving the DMA more breathing
2026-03-29 20:29:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] room.
2026-03-29 20:29:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 4. DMA/Timing Synchronization: Because the PIO will now consume FIFO data during the active
2026-03-29 20:29:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] line but not during the blanking periods, your DMA transfers will need to be perfectly synchronized
2026-03-29 20:29:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] to provide exactly the right amount of data per line. Autopull will stall the state machine if the
2026-03-29 20:29:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] FIFO is empty when an `out` executes, which could throw off your strict video timing.
2026-03-29 20:29:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
