2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] To transition to using `out` for your pixel data, here are the necessary modifications for your PIO
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] setup:
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] • In the PIO Assembly (`.pio`):*
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1. Replace SET with OUT: Swap your `set pindirs, X` instructions in the `stripe` loop with
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] `out pindirs, 1` (shifting 1 bit at a time).
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. Cycle Timing: Adjust the delay cycles on the `out` instructions to maintain your
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 7,800-cycle active line duration based on your new pixel clock.
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 3. Data Fetching: The OSR needs data. It is highly recommended to rely on system Autopull
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] rather than adding explicit `pull` instructions, which would consume valuable cycles and
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] instruction space in your tight loop.
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] • In the C++ Configuration (`.cpp`):*
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1. Pin Mapping: Map the `OUT` pins to your video pin, just as you did for the `SET` pins.
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. Shift Register Config: Configure the `OUT` shift register. You will need to enable
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] Autopull, choose the shift direction (MSB or LSB first depending on your frame buffer layout), and
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] set the pull threshold (typically 32 bits).
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 3. FIFO/DMA Feeding: Ensure your DMA channel is configured and started so it continuously
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] feeds the state machine's TX FIFO. If the OSR empties and the FIFO is dry, the state machine will
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] stall mid-scanline.
2026-03-29 20:30:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] To make the `out pindirs` instructions work, you'll need the following state machine configuration
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] modifications in your C++ setup:
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1. Map OUT pins:
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] Add `smconfigsetoutpins(&config, VID_PIN, 1);` so the `out` instruction knows which
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] GPIO to target. (It shares the same mapping as `out pins`).
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. Configure OSR shift and Autopull:
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] Add `smconfigsetoutshift(&config, true, true, 32);` (shift right, autopull true,
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] 32-bit threshold). This ensures the OSR automatically fetches the next 32-bit word from the TX FIFO
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] without wasting cycles on manual `pull` instructions.
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] 3. Join FIFOs (Highly Recommended):
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] Add `smconfigsetfifojoin(&config, PIOFIFOJOIN_TX);`. Since you don't need
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] the RX FIFO, this combines them into a single 8-word deep TX FIFO, giving your DMA double the
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] breathing room to prevent underflows.
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] On the PIO side, your modified loop looks good. Because you are using autopull, you don't need any
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] extra PIO instructions to fetch the DMA data; it will seamlessly stream into the OSR as long as the
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] DMA keeps the TX FIFO fed.
2026-03-29 20:33:55 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
