2026-03-29 20:47:52 [gemini-3.1-pro] The setup looks solid. The xorshift PRNG is nice and fast, and the non-blocking loop is exactly
2026-03-29 20:47:52 [gemini-3.1-pro] what you need to keep feeding the TX FIFO while still blinking the LED.
2026-03-29 20:47:52 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 20:47:52 [gemini-3.1-pro] Because you enabled `autopull` in the config, the `out pindirs, 1` instructions in your PIO's
2026-03-29 20:47:52 [gemini-3.1-pro] `stripe` loop will automatically fetch your noise words from the TX FIFO into the OSR whenever it
2026-03-29 20:47:52 [gemini-3.1-pro] empties. No extra PIO instructions required.
2026-03-29 20:47:52 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 20:47:52 [gemini-3.1-pro] One minor thing to watch for: pushing 32-bit words at 1.17 MHz (to keep up with a 4-cycle pixel
2026-03-29 20:47:52 [gemini-3.1-pro] loop) gives the ARM core about 128 clock cycles per word. The xorshift is fast enough, but if the
2026-03-29 20:47:52 [gemini-3.1-pro] loop ever falls behind, the PIO will simply stall on the `out` instruction. This might cause a
2026-03-29 20:47:52 [gemini-3.1-pro] slight sync jitter for now, but it will absolutely get noise on the screen.
2026-03-29 20:47:52 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-29 20:47:52 [gemini-3.1-pro] You are good to run it! Let me know if you get a snowy picture.
