2026-03-30 06:05:22 [nitro@ryzen5] will out wait for data?
2026-03-30 06:05:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] No, the `out` instruction does not inherently wait for new data. Executing `out isr, 32` will
2026-03-30 06:05:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] immediately shift 32 bits from the Output Shift Register (OSR) into the Input Shift Register (ISR),
2026-03-30 06:05:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] regardless of whether new data has been provided.
2026-03-30 06:05:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 06:05:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] It will only stall and wait for data under a specific condition: if you have Autopull
2026-03-30 06:05:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] enabled in your state machine configuration, the OSR has reached its shift threshold, and the TX
2026-03-30 06:05:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] FIFO is currently empty.
2026-03-30 06:05:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 06:05:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] If Autopull is disabled, you must use a `pull` instruction (which blocks by default) to wait for
2026-03-30 06:05:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] and load new data from the TX FIFO into the OSR before executing your `out` instruction.
2026-03-30 06:05:34 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 06:06:13 [nitro@ryzen5] autopull is enabled and fifo is empty
2026-03-30 06:06:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] Yes, the state machine will wait (stall).
2026-03-30 06:06:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 06:06:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] Because autopull is enabled, executing the `out` instruction when the Output Shift Register (OSR)
2026-03-30 06:06:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] lacks sufficient bits automatically triggers a `pull` operation. Since the TX FIFO is empty, this
2026-03-30 06:06:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] automatic pull will block and stall the state machine until new data is written to the FIFO.
2026-03-30 06:06:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 06:07:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] Yes, the state machine will wait (stall).
2026-03-30 06:07:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 06:07:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] When `autopull` is enabled and the Output Shift Register (OSR) reaches its configured threshold (32
2026-03-30 06:07:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] bits in your case), the PIO automatically executes a blocking `pull`. Because the TX FIFO
2026-03-30 06:07:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] is empty, the state machine will stall at the `out isr, 32` instruction until new data is provided
2026-03-30 06:07:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] to the FIFO by your C++ program.
2026-03-30 06:07:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 06:07:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] Once you write to the TX FIFO using `piosmput()`, the OSR will instantly refill, and the
2026-03-30 06:07:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] `out` instruction will complete.
2026-03-30 06:07:23 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
