2026-03-30 09:38:39 [nitro@ryzen5] can you check my numbers for new stripe loop
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] Here is a breakdown of the cycle math for your new stripe loop. There is a slight arithmetic error
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] in the comments, a small cycle deficit for the full line, and a critical register collision to
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] watch out for.
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] • 1. Arithmetic & Cycle Count*
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] • Active Loop Math: 704 × 11 cycles is 7,744, not 7,704.
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] • Active Video Total: 3 setup cycles + 7,744 loop cycles = 7,747 cycles.
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] • HBlank Total: 3 setup + 224 (front porch) + 2 setup + 704 (hsync) + 2 setup + 864 (back
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] porch) + 23 (return jump) = 1,822 cycles.
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] • Total Line Time: 7,747 + 1,822 = 9,569 cycles.
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] At 150MHz, a standard 64µs PAL line requires exactly 9,600 cycles. Your current timing is 31
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] cycles short. You can easily perfectly pad this by adding delays to your non-looping
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] instructions (for example, increasing the final `jmp x--` delay to `[31]` and adding `[22]` to `set
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] y, 6`).
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] • 2. Register Collision (`y` loop counter)*
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] Your PIO code initializes `isr` with 311 at the start of the frame (`frame[0]`).
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] During the active video setup, you call `mov y, isr`. This sets `y` to 311, meaning your `stripe`
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] loop will only execute 312 times, not the intended 704 times.
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] Because the loop terminates early, it will only consume 312 bits (9.75 words) per line instead of
2026-03-30 09:40:16 [gemini-3.1-pro] the 704 bits (22 words) your C code pushes. This will immediately cause the TX FIFO to desync. You
