2026-03-30 10:08:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] phosphor flicker seen on CRTs. Instead, the TV will capture the incoming fields and pass them
2026-03-30 10:08:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] through its internal deinterlacer to display a progressive image.
2026-03-30 10:08:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-03-30 10:08:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] To successfully achieve a 704x576 interlaced display, the TV's sync separator must recognize the
2026-03-30 10:08:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] signal as 576i rather than 288p. This requires the standard half-line offset between alternating
2026-03-30 10:08:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] fields.
2026-03-30 10:08:24 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
