2026-03-30 12:01:13 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 12:04:19 [nitro@ryzen5] local jaycar does not seem to have socket for 3.5mm TRRS
2026-03-30 12:04:28 [claude-opus-4-6] You could just solder directly to a TRRS plug instead, or cut your AV cable and splice in.
2026-03-30 12:04:28 [claude-opus-4-6] Alternatively:
2026-03-30 12:04:28 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 12:04:28 [claude-opus-4-6] - A standard 3.5mm TRS socket will physically accept the TRRS plug - it just shorts ring 2 (video)
2026-03-30 12:04:28 [claude-opus-4-6] to sleeve (ground). You could use two sockets: one TRS for stereo audio on tip/ring1, and your
2026-03-30 12:04:28 [claude-opus-4-6] existing GPIO 28 connection for video separately.
2026-03-30 12:04:28 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 12:04:28 [claude-opus-4-6] - A 4-pin header and some hot glue works on the bench.
2026-03-30 12:04:28 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 12:04:28 [claude-opus-4-6] - AliExpress/eBay has TRRS panel mount sockets cheaply if you can wait for shipping.
2026-03-30 12:04:28 [claude-opus-4-6] 
