2026-03-30 13:56:27 [nitro@ryzen5] so no pull up or down on internal gpio?
2026-03-30 13:56:34 [claude-opus-4-6] No, the resistive divider handles the biasing externally. PWM output swings 0–3.3V, the 1kΩ/10kΩ
2026-03-30 13:56:34 [claude-opus-4-6] divides it down to ~300mV peak which is line level.
2026-03-30 13:56:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 13:56:34 [claude-opus-4-6] If you wanted to save a resistor you could use the internal pull-down (~50kΩ on RP2350) but it's
2026-03-30 13:56:34 [claude-opus-4-6] too high impedance and too imprecise for a clean voltage divider. The external 10kΩ is more
2026-03-30 13:56:34 [claude-opus-4-6] predictable.
2026-03-30 13:56:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 13:56:34 [claude-opus-4-6] No pull-up needed - you want the signal biased around 0V for AC-coupled audio inputs, which this
2026-03-30 13:56:34 [claude-opus-4-6] gives you.
2026-03-30 13:56:34 [claude-opus-4-6] 
