2026-03-30 16:30:56 [nitro@ryzen5] what is limit on frequence, the full 32 bit stereo sample, or the bits being sent?
2026-03-30 16:31:03 [claude-opus-4-6] The limit is on BCK - the PCM5102 specs max 50.4MHz for the bit clock.
2026-03-30 16:31:03 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:31:03 [claude-opus-4-6] Your BCK is 3MHz, well within spec. The sample rate is just a consequence:
2026-03-30 16:31:03 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:31:03 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:31:03 [claude-opus-4-6] BCK / bits per sample frame = sample rate
2026-03-30 16:31:03 [claude-opus-4-6] 3MHz / 64 = 46,875 Hz
2026-03-30 16:31:03 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:31:03 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:31:03 [claude-opus-4-6] The 64 comes from 16 bits × 2 channels × 2 PIO cycles per bit (your 4-instruction loop). If you
2026-03-30 16:31:03 [claude-opus-4-6] wanted higher sample rate you could either increase BCK or reduce bit depth - but 46,875 Hz is
2026-03-30 16:31:03 [claude-opus-4-6] plenty for a synth.
2026-03-30 16:31:03 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:10 [nitro@ryzen5] if we stuck with pure 150mhz, could we not use nops for timing?
2026-03-30 16:32:21 [claude-opus-4-6] You could, but why? The clock divider gives you exact timing with zero jitter. NOPs would waste
2026-03-30 16:32:21 [claude-opus-4-6] instruction space and you only have 32 instructions per PIO program.
2026-03-30 16:32:21 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:21 [claude-opus-4-6] At 150MHz undivided, your 4-instruction loop gives:
2026-03-30 16:32:21 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:21 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:21 [claude-opus-4-6] 150MHz / 4 = 37.5MHz BCK - within the 50.4MHz limit
2026-03-30 16:32:21 [claude-opus-4-6] 37.5MHz / 32 = 1,171,875 Hz sample rate - way over 384kHz DAC max
2026-03-30 16:32:21 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:21 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:21 [claude-opus-4-6] You'd need 10 NOPs per loop iteration to get back down to 46,875 Hz. That's 14 instructions per
2026-03-30 16:32:21 [claude-opus-4-6] bit, 14 × 32 = 448 instructions per sample frame - won't fit.
2026-03-30 16:32:21 [claude-opus-4-6] 
