2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] Good point. With delays on existing instructions at 150MHz undivided:
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 150MHz / (N cycles per bit × 32 bits) = sample rate
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] For 48,000 Hz: 150MHz / 48000 / 32 = 97.65 cycles per bit - not integer.
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] For 46,875 Hz: 150MHz / 46875 / 32 = 100 cycles per bit. That's your current setup (divider 25 × 4
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] instructions = 100).
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] For a standard rate, try 37,500 Hz:
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 150MHz / 37500 / 32 = 125 cycles per bit
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 4 instructions + delay of 121 spread across them
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] Or 50,000 Hz from your earlier list:
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 150MHz / 50000 / 32 = 93.75 - no
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] • 75,000 Hz*:
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:56 [claude-opus-4-6] 150MHz / 75000 / 32 = 62.5 - no
2026-03-30 16:32:57 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:57 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:32:57 [claude-opus-4-6] 150MHz just doesn't divide cleanly to standard audio rates at 32 bits per frame. 46,875 Hz is
2026-03-30 16:32:57 [claude-opus-4-6] actually the cleanest you'll get. It's not janky - it's exact at your clock speed.
2026-03-30 16:32:57 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:33:37 [nitro@ryzen5] i dont care about bit rate, we are going for sample rate
2026-03-30 16:33:43 [claude-opus-4-6] Right, sorry. The sample rate is what matters for your synth. 46,875 Hz is exact and clean:
2026-03-30 16:33:43 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:33:43 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:33:43 [claude-opus-4-6] 150MHz / 3200 = 46,875 Hz
2026-03-30 16:33:43 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:33:43 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:33:43 [claude-opus-4-6] No jitter, no fractional divider, your oscillators and filters can work in exact integer ratios of
2026-03-30 16:33:43 [claude-opus-4-6] the clock. That's better than 44,100 or 48,000 which would need fractional dividers and introduce
2026-03-30 16:33:43 [claude-opus-4-6] jitter.
2026-03-30 16:33:43 [claude-opus-4-6] 
2026-03-30 16:33:43 [claude-opus-4-6] 46,875 Hz it is. C setup code next?
